1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,750
I weigh ninety kilos.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,561
I train six days a week.

3
00:00:03,811 --> 00:00:06,287
And last month, I lost an arm-wrestling

4
00:00:06,137 --> 00:00:08,076
match to a guy who weighs sixty.

5
00:00:08,347 --> 00:00:09,392
His name is Kabir.

6
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:10,813
Skinny arms.

7
00:00:10,716 --> 00:00:11,603
No pump.

8
00:00:11,611 --> 00:00:12,697
No supplements.

9
00:00:12,947 --> 00:00:15,045
He beat me in four seconds.

10
00:00:16,789 --> 00:00:18,128
So I asked him to do it

11
00:00:17,979 --> 00:00:18,517
again.

12
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:19,761
He beat me again.

13
00:00:20,011 --> 00:00:21,854
Then he did twenty pull-ups like it

14
00:00:21,705 --> 00:00:22,654
was nothing.

15
00:00:22,926 --> 00:00:24,255
I couldn't sleep that night.

16
00:00:24,926 --> 00:00:26,349
How is a guy with half my

17
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,538
muscle stronger than me?

18
00:00:27,811 --> 00:00:29,255
The answer is not muscle.

19
00:00:29,505 --> 00:00:31,982
It's three things almost nobody trains.

20
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:33,539
And by the end of this video,

21
00:00:33,537 --> 00:00:34,655
I'll show you what happened in the

22
00:00:34,505 --> 00:00:35,224
rematch.

23
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,833
Here's the first thing I learned.

24
00:00:39,084 --> 00:00:40,918
A muscle doesn't move by itself.

25
00:00:41,168 --> 00:00:42,824
Your brain sends a signal down your

26
00:00:42,674 --> 00:00:45,065
nerves, and that signal decides how much

27
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:46,729
of the muscle actually fires.

28
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,760
Every muscle is made of thousands of

29
00:00:48,611 --> 00:00:49,434
little units.

30
00:00:49,684 --> 00:00:51,350
A beginner can only switch on part

31
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,391
of them at the same time.

32
00:00:52,642 --> 00:00:53,918
The rest just sit there.

33
00:00:54,189 --> 00:00:56,150
Years of heavy lifting teach your nervous

34
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,655
system to switch on more of them,

35
00:00:57,716 --> 00:00:59,339
faster, all at once.

36
00:00:59,611 --> 00:01:01,161
Kabir's muscles are smaller.

37
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,476
But when he pulls, almost all of

38
00:01:03,326 --> 00:01:04,118
it fires.

39
00:01:04,367 --> 00:01:06,255
Mine had more muscle and a worse

40
00:01:06,105 --> 00:01:06,771
connection.

41
00:01:07,042 --> 00:01:10,118
So you bought a sports car and

42
00:01:09,968 --> 00:01:11,297
never learned to drive.

43
00:01:11,568 --> 00:01:12,224
Exactly.

44
00:01:13,126 --> 00:01:15,139
So I asked Kabir how he trains.

45
00:01:15,389 --> 00:01:17,466
His answer made me feel stupid.

46
00:01:17,737 --> 00:01:19,055
I train like a bodybuilder.

47
00:01:19,305 --> 00:01:21,550
Ten to fifteen reps, chase the burn,

48
00:01:21,568 --> 00:01:22,582
chase the pump.

49
00:01:22,853 --> 00:01:24,129
Kabir does the opposite.

50
00:01:24,379 --> 00:01:25,108
Heavy weight.

51
00:01:25,274 --> 00:01:26,403
Three to five reps.

52
00:01:26,484 --> 00:01:27,339
Long rest.

53
00:01:27,589 --> 00:01:29,024
He never chases the burn.

54
00:01:29,295 --> 00:01:31,118
High reps mostly build size.

55
00:01:31,368 --> 00:01:33,697
Heavy low reps mostly build strength.

56
00:01:33,947 --> 00:01:36,182
Both build muscle, but only one teaches

57
00:01:36,032 --> 00:01:38,045
your body to lift something really heavy.

58
00:01:38,316 --> 00:01:39,550
Strength is a skill.

59
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,255
You get good at what you practice.

60
00:01:41,505 --> 00:01:42,992
I practiced getting a pump.

61
00:01:43,242 --> 00:01:44,529
He practiced being strong.

62
00:01:46,905 --> 00:01:48,371
The third clue was on his hands.

63
00:01:48,621 --> 00:01:49,866
His fingers were thick.

64
00:01:50,095 --> 00:01:51,982
His forearms looked like cables.

65
00:01:52,253 --> 00:01:54,413
Kabir grew up climbing rocks and carrying

66
00:01:54,263 --> 00:01:56,139
bricks on his uncle's construction site.

67
00:01:56,411 --> 00:01:58,603
Years of that made his tendons strong.

68
00:01:58,853 --> 00:02:00,634
Tendons are the cables that connect muscle

69
00:02:00,484 --> 00:02:01,045
to bone.

70
00:02:01,295 --> 00:02:04,582
Stiffer cables pass force faster, with less

71
00:02:04,432 --> 00:02:05,466
lost on the way.

72
00:02:05,737 --> 00:02:07,329
Muscle grows in weeks.

73
00:02:07,505 --> 00:02:09,729
Tendons take months and years.

74
00:02:09,979 --> 00:02:11,624
That's why the strongest grip in the

75
00:02:11,474 --> 00:02:13,571
gym often belongs to the guy who

76
00:02:13,421 --> 00:02:14,792
looks the least impressive.

77
00:02:17,116 --> 00:02:19,887
And there's one thing neither of us

78
00:02:19,737 --> 00:02:20,824
can change.

79
00:02:21,074 --> 00:02:22,118
Leverage.

80
00:02:22,389 --> 00:02:24,676
Shorter forearms and tendons that attach a

81
00:02:24,526 --> 00:02:26,434
little further from the joint give some

82
00:02:26,284 --> 00:02:28,929
people a natural advantage, like a longer

83
00:02:28,779 --> 00:02:30,076
handle on a wrench.

84
00:02:30,347 --> 00:02:32,476
Kabir has short forearms.

85
00:02:32,726 --> 00:02:34,729
In arm wrestling, that's a cheat code.

86
00:02:34,979 --> 00:02:36,676
You can't train that.

87
00:02:36,926 --> 00:02:38,361
But the first three, you can.

88
00:02:40,737 --> 00:02:41,624
So I made a plan.

89
00:02:41,874 --> 00:02:42,645
Eight weeks.

90
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:43,761
Three changes.

91
00:02:44,032 --> 00:02:44,518
One.

92
00:02:44,768 --> 00:02:46,087
Heavy and low.

93
00:02:46,337 --> 00:02:47,992
Three days a week, three to five

94
00:02:47,842 --> 00:02:49,561
reps on the big lifts, with three

95
00:02:49,411 --> 00:02:50,455
minutes of rest.

96
00:02:50,726 --> 00:02:51,434
Two.

97
00:02:51,684 --> 00:02:53,076
Grip every day.

98
00:02:53,326 --> 00:02:55,845
Dead hangs, towel hangs, farmer carries.

99
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:56,834
Three.

100
00:02:57,084 --> 00:02:59,171
Practice the actual skill.

101
00:02:59,421 --> 00:03:01,782
Twice a week, I arm-wrestled anyone who

102
00:03:01,632 --> 00:03:02,592
would say yes.

103
00:03:02,863 --> 00:03:05,371
You lost to the gym's receptionist.

104
00:03:05,642 --> 00:03:06,266
Twice.

105
00:03:06,116 --> 00:03:07,782
We don't talk about it.

106
00:03:10,368 --> 00:03:11,224
Eight weeks later.

107
00:03:11,474 --> 00:03:12,255
Same table.

108
00:03:12,505 --> 00:03:13,161
Same guy.

109
00:03:13,432 --> 00:03:14,245
He went first.

110
00:03:14,495 --> 00:03:15,255
I didn't move.

111
00:03:15,505 --> 00:03:16,318
Five seconds.

112
00:03:16,568 --> 00:03:17,371
Ten seconds.

113
00:03:17,642 --> 00:03:19,771
Fifteen seconds in, I felt it.

114
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:21,666
Everything fired at once.

115
00:03:22,779 --> 00:03:23,382
And I won.

116
00:03:23,653 --> 00:03:25,476
Then Kabir pointed at the pull-up bar

117
00:03:25,326 --> 00:03:26,013
and said:

118
00:03:26,263 --> 00:03:27,045
best of three.

119
00:03:27,316 --> 00:03:28,150
I lost that one.

120
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:29,708
I'm still not a fan of pull-ups.

121
00:03:31,453 --> 00:03:32,276
Here's what I learned.

122
00:03:32,526 --> 00:03:33,855
Muscle is the engine.

123
00:03:34,105 --> 00:03:36,382
Your nerves are the driver, your tendons

124
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:38,403
are the cables, and your training decides

125
00:03:38,253 --> 00:03:39,350
which one you build.

126
00:03:39,621 --> 00:03:41,245
If you want to look strong, chase

127
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:41,676
the pump.

128
00:03:41,926 --> 00:03:43,676
If you want to be strong, lift

129
00:03:43,526 --> 00:03:45,645
heavy, train your grip, and practice the

130
00:03:45,495 --> 00:03:46,108
skill.

131
00:03:46,379 --> 00:03:47,455
Tell me in the comments:

132
00:03:47,705 --> 00:03:49,076
have you ever lost to a skinny

133
00:03:48,926 --> 00:03:49,361
guy?

134
00:03:49,611 --> 00:03:50,308
Be honest.
